en:
Yeah?
I like cards too.
You've gotta admit, they're a brilliant invention.{p}

They seemed to have come out of every single card, so there must've been fifty of them.
They all looked at me at once.
And then they started shrieking in shrill voices, eek eek eek eek.{p}

"Gyaah!"
Maybe he fell wrong, but the knife plunged right into Okura's gut.
It happened at the very same instant.{p}

"Hee-hee-hee-hee-hee!"
The women's shrieks of delight rang out.
And they all bit into Okura's belly at once.{p}

Covered in blood, they cackled and squealed with joy.
Some of the heads slit Okura's belly wide open, burrowed inside, and danced around in there.
It was like a huge swarm of ants on a dead insect.{p}

Yeah?
I like cards too.
You've gotta admit, they're a brilliant invention.{p}

Shindo drew three cards from the deck.
"I've got three cards here: the ace, the king and the joker."
As he spoke, he laid them out face down.{p}

All right then, I'll tell you.
It was the card story, right...?
Still, you gotta admit they're really well made.{p}

We got through to the end of the day like that.
But when the final bell rang and everyone was about to leave the classroom,
the ones at the front of the crowd started murmuring.{p}

As I went out the school gate, I nearly crashed into someone walking toward me.
I dodged at the last second, and just as we passed each other, Ishikawa came flying out.
I guess he saw a figure and thought it was me.{p}

There was a shrill scream.
At the same moment, he felt something strange in his right hand.
Out of the corner of his eye he saw Uchida collapse, but Ishikawa couldn't tear his eyes from the thing sitting in his right hand.{p}

Shindo finished his story.
{f:Had he been reminded of that day?|I wondered if he was remembering that day.}
His face {f:looked|seemed} a little pale.
Now that I thought about it, {f:I|I} felt a little sick too{f:.|.}{p}But the next one would be the sixth story{f:.|.}
"Please, go ahead."{p}

"You were trying to scare me.
That's mean."
{f:I|I} protested.
That was going too far. It was just bad taste{f:.|.}
But then Shindo's expression changed.
His smile vanished as if wiped away, and he looked at {f:me|me} with serious eyes.{p}

"Trying to scare you...?
You thought that was a joke?"
His voice was almost a whisper.{p}

I had a bad feeling about this{f:.|.}
It wasn't because Shindo was angry.
If he'd been angry, I'd have felt {f:better.|better, at least.}
Shindo wasn't angry.
He was afraid{f:...!|...!}
Cold sweat trickled down my back.
As {f:I|I} sat there silent, Shindo spoke to me in a quiet voice.{p}

"Good, that's it.
Listen, {a}... no matter what you see, don't freak out."
With that, Shindo took {f:my|my} hand.{p}

For an instant, my vision seemed to lurch and warp.
...But that was all{f:.|.}
There was nothing dangerous like Shindo said, not anywhere...{p}

When I looked up, Shindo was silently staring at something.
Was he looking at... {f:my|my} lap?
Copying him, {f:I|I} lowered my gaze too.{p}

"But isn't this perfect for livening up your project?
You getting possessed right here, while we're telling our stories...
Well then, guess I'll pass it on to the next one."{p}

The moment he said it, there was a sharp crack, like something bursting.
And not just once, but again and again, from all over the room{f:!|!}
"See... you said something so stupid, now they're laughing at you."{p}

Laughing?
By 'they,' does he mean the ghosts{f:?|?}
{f:Is|Is} this spirit rapping★{p}

What's that supposed to mean?
{f:If you're a man, give me a straight answer|Say it more clearly}, will ya.
If you like it, you like it. If you hate it, you hate it.{p}

"Guess I was the one they chose."
Saying something like that, he went home all chipper.
And he never came to school again.{p}

Suddenly, he let out a scream.
"It's over!
Time's up☆"{p}

And from inside, they heard a dry, rustling sound.
Wondering what it was, they opened the door.
And then...{p}

All that was left, they say, was Okura's skeleton and the pure white cards the women had crawled out of.
It must not have been Okura eating the food at all, but those women.
With the family gone and no meals set out, the starving women must've eaten Okura instead.{p}

Then the old man said something to him, and he trudged off like he'd given up.
I went after him.
I caught up with him on the grounds of a deserted shrine and called out to him.{p}

He had a knife raised over his head.
His bloodshot eyes were glaring right at me.
"Stop it☆"{p}

Okura started the ritual.
He drew a magic circle with some kind of powder and chanted a spell.
Then a mist began to fill the dark classroom.{p}

It looked like they'd come out of every single card, so there must've been about fifty of them.
All at once, they looked at me.
Then they started crying in high, shrill voices. Squee, squee, squee, squee.{p}

"Gyaah!"
Maybe he fell wrong, but the knife plunged right into Okura's gut.
It happened at the very same instant.{p}

"Hee-hee-hee-hee-hee!"
The women's shrieks of delight rang out.
And they all bit into Okura's belly at once.{p}

Covered in blood, they cackled and squealed with joy.
Some of the heads slit Okura's belly wide open, burrowed inside, and danced around in there.
It was like a huge swarm of ants on a dead insect.{p}

"It's the joker☆"
Shindo cried out happily.
It didn't feel great, but if it set Shindo's mind at ease, {f:I guess|I suppose} I could live with it.{p}

Just as {f:I|I} thought that, something small flashed across my vision.
{f:What was that|What was that}?
I followed it with my eyes, and {f:I|I} froze.{p}

But the next moment,
{f:I|I} froze.
{f:There|Right there}, at Shindo's feet, was a tiny creature.{p}
